cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this dataset, please cite it."
type: dataset
title: "Forest Harvest History (wss-forest-harvest)"
abstract: >-
  Weekly point-in-time captures of forest harvest applications from two
  regulators that discard the pending stage of their own pipelines. CAL FIRE
  publishes proposed timber harvest plans for California but keeps no permanent
  record of plans that are withdrawn. Skogsstyrelsen publishes Swedish felling
  notifications that age out of the live service after roughly five years,
  while retaining performed harvests back to 1979. Both regulators keep what
  was completed and delete what was abandoned, so withdrawal and expiry leave
  no trace in the official record. This dataset preserves each week's state of
  both pending queues as the bytes were served, with a manifest row recording
  the URL, fetch time and SHA-256 of every capture.
authors:
  - name: "neldivad"
    website: "https://github.com/neldivad"
  - name: "q3dresearch"
    website: "https://github.com/q3dresearch"
license: CC-BY-4.0
# Concept DOI: always resolves to the latest release. Minted 2026-09-07 from
# q3dresearch/wss-forest-harvest via the Zenodo GitHub integration.
#
# This is the SECOND series. The first (10.5281/zenodo.22431866 concept,
# .22431867 for v2026.1) was deleted by the owner on 2026-09-07 and returns
# HTTP 410. Do not cite it. Zenodo permits owner deletion within 30 days of
# publishing, which most registrars deliberately do not.
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.22647878
keywords:
  - forestry
  - timber harvest
  - logging
  - deforestation
  - land use
  - forest policy
